Use the `semantic_view` materialization to define Snowflake Semantic Views in dbt, including tables, relationships, facts, dimensions, and metrics.
Use the `ref()` function for Semantic Views defined in your dbt project, and use `source()` for existing external Semantic Views.

{{ config(materialized='view') }}
select * from semantic_view(
  {{ ref('<semantic_view_model_name>') }}
  METRICS ...
  DIMENSIONS ...
  WHERE ...
)

{{ config(materialized='table') }}
select * from semantic_view(
  {{ source('<source_name>', '<semantic_view>') }}
  METRICS ...
  DIMENSIONS ...
  WHERE ...
)

The `dbt_semantic_view` package includes the following features for defining and managing Snowflake Semantic Views in dbt projects. Use `ref()` for Semantic Views defined in your dbt project, and use `source()` for existing external Semantic Views.

```sql
{{ config(materialized='view') }}
select * from semantic_view(
  {{ ref('<semantic_view_model_name>') }}
  METRICS ...
  DIMENSIONS ...
  WHERE ...
)
```

